      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation Gulbarga Safe</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Shipping a two-wheeler from Gulbarga to any destination in India requires meticulous preparation to ensure a smooth, legally compliant, and damage-free transfer. The foundation of this process lies in providing accurate and verifiable documentation to your transport provider.</p>
<p>Gaps in paperwork can lead to customs delays, legal complications, or refusal of service. To avoid these issues, ensure you have the following essential documents ready before your bike is loaded for transit.</p>

<h3>Essential Bike Transportation Documents</h3>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Self-Attested RC Photocopy:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A clear, color photocopy of the vehicle’s Registration Certificate (RC) is mandatory. This document proves legal ownership. It must be self-attested by your signature and date. If the RC is in a nominee’s name, provide both RC copies and a valid ID proof of the owner.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current PUC Certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A valid Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate is required to confirm your vehicle meets environmental standards. An expired PUC can cause transit delays or rejection by logistics hubs. Keep a digital or physical copy handy.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Provide a copy of your current comprehensive or third-party insurance policy. The policy must cover the entire transit period. If your vehicle is under hypothecation (loan), include a copy of the No Objection Certificate (NOC) from your bank.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA-Approved Consignment Bilty:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">This is the primary freight document issued by the transporter. It details the origin, destination, vehicle description, and agreed charges. Verify all details—especially the vehicle’s registration number, model, and chassis/engine numbers—before signing. Keep the original for customs clearance upon arrival.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>While these documents handle legal compliance, protecting your investment is equally critical. This is where <strong>100% declared-value marine transit insurance</strong> becomes indispensable.</p>

<p>Standard vehicle insurance often excludes transit risks or offers limited coverage. In contrast, marine transit insurance is specifically designed for goods and vehicles in motion.</p>
<p>By opting for <strong>100% declared-value coverage</strong>, you ensure that in the event of an accident, theft, fire, or water damage during transit, you receive a full payout matching your bike’s current market value—not a depreciated or partial amount. This policy typically covers:</p>
<ul>
<li>Physical damage from collisions, overturning, or loading/unloading mishaps.</li>
<li>Theft or robbery during the journey.</li>
<li>Damage due to natural calamities like floods or heavy rain.</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Always request a detailed insurance policy document from your transporter.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Confirm the insurer’s name, policy number, and claim process.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>For high-value bikes, consider adding riders for minor scratches or glass breakage.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>By pairing complete documentation with robust marine insurance, you eliminate financial risk and ensure your bike arrives in Gulbarga’s destination city exactly as it left—secure, insured, and hassle-free.</span></li></ul></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


